.TH XIL\-EPISODE\-SUMMARY "1" "2026\-07\-02" "xil\-pipeline 0.3.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
xil\-episode\-summary \- write a one\-row\-per\-episode summary CSV from all parsed JSON files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B xil\-episode\-summary
[\-h] [\-\-output FILE] [\-\-show NAME] [\-\-stdout]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Scans all
.B parsed_<TAG>.json
files under the current show's
.B parsed/\fR\fI<slug>\fR/
directory and writes a summary CSV with one row per episode.  Columns include
the episode tag, title, total entry count, dialogue count, direction count,
section list, and word count.
.PP
Useful for tracking progress across a season or auditing show\-level metrics.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-output\fR \fI\,FILE\/\fR, \fB\-o\fR \fI\,FILE\/\fR
Write CSV to FILE (default: \fI<workspace>\fR/parsed/\fI<slug>\fR/episode_summary.csv)
.TP
\fB\-\-show\fR \fI\,NAME\/\fR
Show name or slug override (default: resolved from project.json / active show)
.TP
\fB\-\-stdout\fR
Write CSV to stdout \(em no banner, safe to pipe
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Generate a season summary for the active show:
.B xil episode\-summary
.TP
Write to a named file:
.B xil episode\-summary \-\-output season1_summary.csv
.TP
Pipe to column for aligned display:
.B xil episode\-summary \-\-stdout | column \-t \-s,
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR xil (1),
.BR xil\-parse (1),
.BR xil\-parsed\-csv (1),
.BR xil\-status (1)
